(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/id "adr-2609160849-kotoba-cloud-pat-v2-deploy-regression")
  (:adr/title "api.kotoba.cloud 2026-09-16 00:50 JST: every PAT request answered 403 research-access-denied for ten minutes — the edge was deployed from a branch that predates PAT v2")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-09-16")
  (:adr/related (vector "ADR-2609160028" "ADR-2608136000" "ADR-2608135200" "ADR-2609112300"))
  (:adr/context
  "Owner report (2026-09-16, hermes on api.kotoba.cloud): `Compression aborted: Error code: 403 - {'error': {'code': 'research-access-denied'}}` followed by `compression is currently blocked (cooldown:60)`. The question was the cause.

  Where the code is read (orgs/kotoba-lang/app-kotoba-cloud, origin/main d758d757 at the time of reading; the local checkout was 120 commits behind on branch kotoba-proof-biometric-wiring and was NOT used as the source of truth):
  - `research-access-denied` is a code of the edge Worker kotoba-cloud-control-plane (src/app_kotoba_cloud/research_gateway.cljk), never of Anthropic. It is not served on /v1/messages at all (not in research-gateway/paths); the request that carried it was POST /v1/chat/completions with `Authorization: Bearer kc_pat_...` (hermes speaks the OpenAI shape; the error text is the openai python client's APIStatusError format).
  - On the bearer path only two things answer 403 research-access-denied: `pat/verify` returning nil (bearer-auth), and the outer catch's status family for a 403 thrown by an authority hop (edge-error-code). The authority's /status never throws 403 (handle-status), the /tokens/check 403 (token-unknown / token-revoked / legacy-token-revoked) is answered as 401 token-revoked, and a /jobs/create 403 (guardrail-blocked, firewall-denied, eligibility) is answered as 403 research-service-unavailable from complete-via-job's own catch. Body over the limit is 413 body-too-large, an unknown key or model is 400 invalid-research-request, a missing scope is 403 research-scope-required. So a bearer 403 research-access-denied means: the presented token did not pass HMAC/structure verification.
  - PAT v2 (`kc_pat_<principalB64url>.<tokenId 12 hex>.<hmac 16 hex>`, per-token revocation registry on the authority) landed on main in 86b65ef4 (2026-09-15 22:28 JST). The pre-v2 `verify` requires exactly one dot after the prefix (`(= (.lastIndexOf rest \".\") dot)`) and returns nil for a three-part token — before any HMAC is computed.

  Measured (each step reproducible, values not to be quoted as constants):
  1. ~/.hermes/.env KOTOBA_API_TOKEN is a v2 token (3 dot-separated parts after kc_pat_; `grep '^KOTOBA_API_TOKEN=' ~/.hermes/.env | cut -d= -f2- | awk -F. '{print NF}'` prints 3). The backups .env.bak-20260915094549 / -194439 / -224443 hold a v1 token (2 parts): the owner's other session issued the v2 token and put it in .env at 22:45 JST (ADR-2609160028 gap note).
  2. ~/.hermes/logs/agent.log: the first `403 research-access-denied` is at 2026-09-16 00:50:10; from then until 00:58 every api.kotoba.cloud call answered it — the main conversation calls too (`agent.conversation_loop: API call failed ... base_url=https://api.kotoba.cloud/v1 model=qwen3.8-flash-next-whitehacker summary=HTTP 403`), not only the compression summary. The compression warning was merely the first line on screen. At 01:03 the same token got a 429 (research-service-unavailable) — i.e. it passed verification again.
  3. `npx wrangler deployments list --name kotoba-cloud-control-plane`: a deployment at 2026-09-15T15:50:08Z = 00:50:08 JST (version 7c529a30, author the owner's Cloudflare account, message empty), then 16:00:17Z and 16:05:09Z. The 403 window starts in the same minute as the first and ends with the second.
  4. Of every app-kotoba-cloud commit between 00:39 and 01:05 JST, `git show <sha>:src/app_kotoba_cloud/pat.cljk | grep -c hmac-domain-v2` is non-zero for all except the kotoba-proof-biometric-wiring branch (657eaafb 09-15 20:31, 2acf54f6 00:52, 1c5b60d0 00:55, a6649c55 01:02 — zero each) until its merge of main at 141f3a69 (01:04). That branch was checked out in the shared orgs/kotoba-lang/app-kotoba-cloud checkout, whose build/ directory was written at 00:46. This is consistent with — not proof of — the 00:50 deploy having been built from that checkout; the deployment carries no source reference (`Source: Unknown`).
  5. Live now (no quota consumed): POST /v1/chat/completions with the .env token and a body without messages answers 400 `messages: not an array` (authentication passed); GET /v1/research/status answers 200 status eligible. A deliberately malformed kc_pat_ token answers 403 research-access-denied; a non-PAT bearer answers 403 origin-not-allowed. The live edge therefore verifies v2 tokens again; the regression lasted from the 00:50 deploy to the 01:00 deploy.
  6. hermes routed the compression summary to api.kotoba.cloud: `Auxiliary compression: using custom (claude-sonnet-5) at https://api.kotoba.cloud/v1/` (00:56:26, 00:58:16) although ~/.hermes/config.yaml (mtime 23:41, before that session) says auxiliary.compression.base_url http://127.0.0.1:9180/v1 (scripts/claude-bridge.cljs, alive, serves claude-sonnet-5) with no `provider:` key. The edge's OpenAI-compatible validator refuses a model outside its catalog as 400 `model: unknown id` before reserving a job — so once verification works, that compression call fails with 400 instead of 403.")
  (:adr/decision
  "No code change in this session; the regression had already been undone by the later deploys before the question was asked. What is decided and recorded:
  - The cause is a production deploy of kotoba-cloud-control-plane from a checkout that did not contain origin/main (CLAUDE.md Git operations: deploys only from a checkout that includes origin/main; hook wrangler-deploy-main-sync-guard.cljs). The hook guards Claude Code sessions only — a Codex session or a bare `wrangler deploy` from a terminal is not stopped. Between 00:47 and 01:05 JST at least six worktrees of this repo (/private/tmp/akc-*, scratchpad wt/akc*) were deploying the same Worker minutes apart (last deploy wins); a deploy from any of them that lacked 86b65ef4 reproduces the failure for every v2 token holder.
  - The symptom to recognise next time: a bearer 403 research-access-denied that starts in the same minute as a deploy and hits every request, while /v1/research/status with the same token answered 200 minutes earlier. Check `pat.cljk` of the deployed source for hmac-domain-v2 before touching tokens or secrets. Rotating PAT_SIGNING_SECRET would have made it worse (every token invalid).
  - The hermes-side finding (measurement 6) is an open gap, not fixed here: the owner was asked whether to set `provider: custom` explicitly on auxiliary.compression / approval / mcp / triage_specifier in ~/.hermes/config.yaml and did not answer before closing; personal config is not edited without that answer.

  Verification fixed: no test suite was run because no code changed. The evidence is the five reproducible measurements above (log grep, wrangler deployments list, per-commit grep of pat.cljk, two live probes with the owner's token that reserve no job, one probe with a malformed token). The local app-kotoba-cloud checkout's own build (build/worker.js, 01:08) contains hmac-domain-v2 — it is on the branch after its 01:04 merge of main.")
  (:adr/body
  "Remaining gaps, by priority:
  1. hermes compression still routes to api.kotoba.cloud with model claude-sonnet-5 (measurement 6) → will answer 400 model: unknown id. Fix candidate: in ~/.hermes/config.yaml add `provider: custom` under auxiliary.compression (and approval, mcp, triage_specifier, which share the 127.0.0.1:9180 shape). Confirm by the log line `Auxiliary compression: using custom (claude-sonnet-5) at http://127.0.0.1:9180/v1/` in ~/.hermes/logs/agent.log after the next auto-compression, or by `/compress`. Hermes source: ~/.hermes/hermes-agent/agent/auxiliary_client.py `_resolve_task_provider_model` (docstring: a bare base_url means custom, a first-class provider + base_url keeps the provider identity) — the observed route says the provider identity won.
  2. Deploy governance: nothing prevents a non-Claude-Code session from deploying kotoba-cloud-control-plane from a stale checkout. Candidates, not decided: a `wrangler deploy` wrapper in app-kotoba-cloud (package.json script) that refuses unless `git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/main HEAD` after a fetch; or the edge answering its own source sha on /health so a deploy can be attributed (today `Source: Unknown`, message empty).
  3. The shared checkout orgs/kotoba-lang/app-kotoba-cloud is on branch kotoba-proof-biometric-wiring (moving: 40043fee → c09d3c5a during this session) with tracked changes (cljk-origin.edn, package.json, src/app_kotoba_cloud/site.cljk) and untracked assets/enforcement-catalog* — owner WIP of another live session, not touched, not synced to the west pin.

  Resume point (next agent, no history needed):
  - grep -c 'research-access-denied' ~/.hermes/logs/agent.log   (a rising count after a deploy = the same class; then `npx wrangler deployments list --name kotoba-cloud-control-plane` from orgs/kotoba-lang/app-kotoba-cloud and compare minutes)
  - T=$(grep '^KOTOBA_API_TOKEN=' ~/.hermes/.env | cut -d= -f2-); curl -s -w ' %{http_code}\n' https://api.kotoba.cloud/v1/research/status -H \"authorization: Bearer $T\"   (expect 200 eligible; a 403 research-access-denied here is the token failing verification, a 401 token-revoked is the registry)
  - gap 1: edit ~/.hermes/config.yaml as above, run hermes, read the `Auxiliary compression: using` line.

  Owner WIP preserved, not touched: the biometric-wiring checkout above; worktrees /private/tmp/akc-docs-graph, akc-enforcement, akc-pr-merge/{106,129,207}, csf-worktree, ra-fix and two scratchpad wt/akc* of another session; ~/.hermes/config.yaml and .env unchanged; no stash created; no branch of anyone else moved.")
))
